# DHH23 – Helsinki Digital Humanities Hackathon 2023

**Authors:** David Bordon

## Abstract
<jats:p>Report from the Helsinki Digital Humanities Hackathon 2023 (DHH23), which took place at the end of May 2023. The hackathon serves as a practical demonstration platform for the University of Helsinki's approach to teaching digital humanities. The event promotes collaboration between humanities and computer science researchers, profiles that have divergent visions of science and are the product of completely different traditions. The author strongly recommends that everyone who is at the beginning of their research career should plan to attend.</jats:p>

**Source:** https://doi.org/10.4312/slo2.0.2023.2.92-101

